  <PageIntro
    number="05"
    title="About"
    description="I’m Gabriel I. Alonso. I explore the connections between geometry, computation, and visual expression."
  />
  <div class="about-layout">
    <div class="about-text">
      <p>
        My full name is Gabriel Isaac Alonso Serrato, and I also make things as <em
          >Arthifact</em
        >. My background brings together computer science and environmental
        engineering; my research direction is geometry processing.
      </p><p>
        I’m interested in how geometric representations connect to simulation
        and computer graphics. During the Summer Geometry Initiative in 2025, I
        explored differentiable meshing and co-authored an <a
          href="https://summergeometry.org/sgi2025/dmesh/">essay on DMesh++</a
        >.
      </p><p>
        Alongside research, I build interactive systems and open-source tools,
        and create 3D art and animation. This site collects that work, together
        with the notes I make along the way.
      </p>
    </div>
